  "text": "SYNTHETIC TEST DOCUMENT - not a real patient. Written for CPT Studio participant tests.\nGI Procedure Report\nDate of service: 2026-10-21\nProcedure: Colonoscopy.\nIndication: Average-risk screening.\nTechnique: The colonoscope was advanced to the cecum. The appendiceal orifice and the ileocecal valve were\nidentified. Bowel preparation was good.\nFindings: A 6 mm sessile polyp in the ascending colon was removed with a cold snare and retrieved for\npathology. A 3 mm polyp in the rectum was biopsied with cold forceps.\nImpression: Two polyps; one removed by cold snare, one biopsied.\nPlan: Await pathology. Repeat colonoscopy in 7 years.\n",
